# Terraform: Create S3 Bucket with Versioning
main.tf
terraform {
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 6.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-terraform-versioning-bucket-12345"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "versioning" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket.id

  versioning_configuration {
    status = "Enabled"
  }
}
Commands
terraform init
terraform validate
terraform plan
terraform apply

To delete the bucket and resources:

terraform destroy
What happens?
Terraform
   ↓
AWS Provider
   ↓
Create S3 Bucket
   ↓
Enable Versioning
   ↓
S3 Bucket
   ├── File v1
   ├── File v2
   └── File v3

Important: S3 bucket names must be globally unique. Change my-terraform-versioning-bucket-12345 to your own unique name.
